   "date": "2013-06-20",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The coalition supported the Statute Stocktake (Appropriations) Bill 2013, a housekeeping bill repealing 84 redundant appropriation acts from July 1999 to June 2010. It criticised the government's deregulation claims, citing that the Rudd-Gillard Labor governments added about 21,000 new regulations and repealed only 104 since 2008."
